r the sea of Cilician pirates. This mentions sending fleets to specific bodies of water.  \n- Passage 11: USS Greer incident, but not about sending ships to a body of water.  \n- Passage 15: Battle of Ponta Delgada, a combined corsair expedition sailed against a Spanish naval force off the coast of São Miguel in the Azores. Not exactly "sent naval ships to that body of water" by a specific entity? It says "sailed against", but who sent them? The passage says "A combined corsair expedition, mainly French... sailed against a Spanish naval force". So the French sent ships?  \n- Passage 18: French Marines and naval infantry intended for the invasion of northern Germany were dispatched... but that\'s land forces. The French navy abandoned the blockade. Not about sending ships to a body of water.\n\nThe question is likely referring to a specific body of water that is the subject of the question. But the question is standalone: "Who sent naval ships to that body of water' (gold 'Caesar')
