s the autumn storms of the North Sea forced the return of more of the French ships, the blockade of the north German ports diminished..." This implies the French sent naval ships to the North Sea to blockade north German ports. So the French sent naval ships to the North Sea.\n\nBut is there a more direct match? Let\'s check passage 19: Rhine empties into the North Sea. No naval ships mentioned.\n\nPassage 0: Battle of Bantam in Bantam Bay, Indonesia. Dutch and Portuguese fleets. Not a specific body of water named in the question.\n\nThe question is likely part of a series where "that body of water" refers to something previously mentioned. Since we only have the passages, we need to infer which body of water is most likely the referent. Often in such datasets, the question is about a specific entity mentioned in one of the passages. The phrase "that body of water" suggests it was mentioned in a previous question or context. But we don\'t have that.\n\nMaybe the question is asking about the body of water mentioned in the passage that is most relevant to naval ships being sent. Let\'s see which passage explicitly mentions sending naval ships to a body' (gold 'Caesar')
