 body? Possibly the Atlantic Ocean, mentioned in many passages. Who sent naval ships to the Atlantic? Passage 2: British sent to South Atlantic. Passage 11: US Navy ship in Battle of the Atlantic. Passage 6: Luftwaffe attacked shipping in the Atlantic. Passage 4: Soviets provided submarine base, access to Northern Sea Route, forced Britain to protect sea lanes in Atlantic and Pacific.\n\nBut the question likely expects a specific answer from a specific passage. Since the question is "Who sent naval ships to that body of water?" and the passages include multiple bodies of water, I need to infer which one is "that body of water". Possibly the Atlantic Ocean is the most frequently mentioned body of water. Who sent naval ships to the Atlantic? The British sent a large force to the South Atlantic (Passage 2). Also the US sent ships in Battle of the Atlantic (Passage 11). But the question asks "Who sent naval ships to that body of water?" – singular.\n\nGiven the passages, the most direct answer is from Passage 2: "The British... sent a large force to track down and destroy the victorious German cruiser squadron."' (gold 'Caesar')
